# Slack notify on finish

When a user task is finished (deck built, upload done, or they asked to be notified), send Slack before ending the turn.

Read and follow `~/.cursor/skills/slack-notification/SKILL.md`.

```bash
source ~/.zshrc 2>/dev/null || true
# Fallback: ~/.config/automation/slack.env
~/.cursor/skills/slack-notification/scripts/send-slack.sh \
  --title "PraisonAIPPT: <short outcome>" \
  --body "<2–5 lines>
View Link: <full https://docs.google.com/... URL>"
```

Always include the Google Drive **View Link** (or **Edit Link** for a Google Doc) when a file was uploaded. If upload was skipped, say why and still send Slack with the local path.

Confirm in chat: "Slack notification sent". Do not log tokens.
